# Kept out of the Composer dist archive. A consumer installs this package to
# use it, never to develop it, so nothing below is worth the download.
#
# What a consumer needs is short: /src, /composer.json, /config, /LICENSE,
# /README.md and /resources. Everything else in the repository is listed below.
#
# /resources holds the Laravel Boost guidelines this package hands to the
# applications that install it. Boost reads them out of the installed package
# directory, so excluding them here would ship a package that offers nothing.
#
# Every path here must exist. Six entries previously named files that had been
# renamed or deleted years earlier (/.phpcs.xml, /.phpmd.xml, /.phpunit.xml,
# /.phpunit.xml.dist, /.scrutinizer.yml, /.travis.yml), so the real config
# files shipped while the list looked complete. Listing a real archive is what
# settles that, not reading the list and not `git check-attr export-ignore`.
# The attribute query reports a file inside an excluded directory as
# unspecified, so it cannot tell a working exclusion from a missing one.
#
# The agent instruction files are excluded from the archive only. Both stay
# tracked, so every clone still receives them.
/.devcontainer export-ignore
/.editorconfig export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.github export-ignore
/.gitignore export-ignore
/.phive export-ignore
/.vscode export-ignore
/AGENTS.md export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
/ISSUE_TEMPLATE.md export-ignore
/SECURITY.md export-ignore
/docker-compose.yml export-ignore
/phive export-ignore
/phpcs.xml.dist export-ignore
/phpmd.xml export-ignore
/phpstan-baseline.neon export-ignore
/phpstan.neon export-ignore
/phpunit.xml.dist export-ignore
/pint.json export-ignore
/tests export-ignore
/tools export-ignore
